iga-nurbs-surface3d-bending.out
NURBS surface of revolution in space with bending: the independent energy derivative
StaticStructural nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 25 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all
ndofman 16 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 16 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 12
# A curved quadratic generatrix (two knot spans along u) revolved by a quarter turn, the quarter circle being an
# exact quadratic NURBS with two knot spans along v (weights 1, (1 + 1/sqrt(2))/2, (1 + 1/sqrt(2))/2, 1), then
# rotated and shifted into a general position; surfacetensionmat2 with all membrane terms and bending
# (omega1 0.7, useh0 1: H0 is the mean curvature of the reference surface), deformed in all three directions
# (not axisymmetrically).
# The 12 dofs of the four interior control points are free; their loads are the reference forces of the target
# configuration, so Newton (manrmsteps 1) has to end there, quadratically; checktangent compares the material
# tangents with finite differences. The boundary control points are prescribed and their reactions checked.
# Reference values: the derivative (complex step) of the total energy integrated with the same Gauss rule
# (4 x 4 per span) from the classical surface quantities of the rational surfaces, independently of the grad F
# formulation and of the rational basis functions of OOFEM (homogeneous form x = sum N w x_A / sum N w):
# metrics A_ab, a_ab, J = sqrt(det a / det A), |F|^2 = A^ab a_ab, normal n = x_,1 x x_,2 / |.|,
# H = a^ab (n . x_,ab) / 2 and likewise H0 with X,
# W = .4 J + .2 |F| + .5 (|F|^2/2 - 1 - ln J) + .6 (ln J)^2/2 + .3 (J - 1)^2/2 + .7/2 J (H - H0)^2.
